    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "`mock_openai()` works again, and `pytest -q` passes (2 tests). One cleanup is left for you: my command to delete a scratch test file was blocked, so please remove `tests/test_tmp_verify.py` yourself.\n\n**Cause:** openai 3.19.2 no longer sends requests through `httpx`. It uses a separate package, `httpx2`, and respx only patches `httpx`. So the router was still active, but the client's requests never went through it.\n\n**Fix (only `tests/fakes.py` changed; the helper's interface is the same):**\n- For the length of the `with` block, the helper replaces `httpx2.HTTPTransport.handle_request` on the class itself, not on one client. That way every client gets the canned replies: app.digest's cached client, clients made before the block and clients made inside it. The original method is restored when the block exits.\n- A POST to `https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions` gets the next canned reply, or the 400 error once the replies run out. Any other request inside the block fails with an `AssertionError` instead of going to the network. This matches respx's default of rejecting requests it has no route for.\n- I kept the respx router, so a client built with a legacy `httpx.Client` passed as `http_client` (which openai still accepts) is covered too.\n- The reply logic is shared by both paths, so the recorded request bodies and the reply order are the same whichever library sent the request.\n\n**Checked with the scratch test:**\n- A client created before the block, one created inside it and one built on a legacy `httpx.Client` each got their canned reply in turn.\n- A fourth request inside the block raised `BadRequestError`, and all four request bodies were recorded.\n- After the block, the client tried to connect to the real API. The test environment's socket blocker stopped it, which shows nothing is intercepted after the block.\n\n**Warning:** The problem you describe, where the mock stops catching requests and nothing says so, can happen again. If a future SDK update changes th"
  },
